{
  "name": "V-NULL-SQL",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "SQL empty text against NULL on PostgreSQL and MariaDB: a parameter given empty text inserts empty text, a parameter given None inserts NULL, the rows read back empty text and null, and a procedure argument given None binds NULL. The Finally path drops the per-run table and procedure on both databases.",
